        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true
        }
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(fountain_stage_count{namespace=\"$namespace\", stage=\"setup\", status=\"failed\"}[1h])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "setup failed"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(increase(fountain_stage_count{namespace=\"$namespace\", stage=\"model\", status=\"failed\"}[1h])) or vector(0)",
          "legendFormat": "model failed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Where the rest of the product questions live",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 42
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "\nThis dashboard answers **how many** and **how fast**, because Prometheus holds\ncounts and durations with no identity attached.\n\nQuestions about **who** and **whether they came back** live in PostHog, on the\n**Fountain / Product** dashboard. Cohorts, retention and per-account funnels\nneed person-level events, which is exactly what `Fountain.Analytics` sends and\nwhat a time series deliberately throws away.\n\nRough split:\n\n| Question | Here | PostHog |\n|---|---|---|\n| How many turns finished this hour | yes | yes |\n| Did last week's signups come back | no | yes |\n| Which accounts hit a model failure | no | yes |\n| Is p95 time-to-first-output regressing | yes | no |\n| Which runtime is slowest | yes | no |\n\nSee `docs/guides/operate/dashboards.md` in the Fountain repo for both.\n"
      }
    }
  ]
}
